From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: Check ADDBA extension bounds before reading fields

parse_addba_option_element() reads the next element length before checking
whether its header fits in the received options. This also reads past the
valid input after the last complete element. An ADDBA extension with zero
payload length reaches Octet[0] without a content byte.

Checking the header before its length field and requiring an extension
content byte keeps parsing within the supplied options. Truncated elements
stop parsing and empty extensions are skipped.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/common/ba_action.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/ba_action.c
@@ -2755,9 +2755,13 @@ void parse_addba_option_element(
 	UINT32 length = 0;
 
 	eid = (PEID_STRUCT) option_ie;
-	while ((length + 2 + eid->Len) <= option_le_len) {
+	while (length + 2 <= option_le_len &&
+	       length + 2 + eid->Len <= option_le_len) {
 		switch (eid->Eid) {
 		case IE_ADDBA_EXT:
+			if (eid->Len < 1)
+				break;
+
 			MTWF_DBG(NULL, DBG_CAT_PROTO, CATPROTO_BA,
 				DBG_LVL_INFO,
 				"- IE_ADDBA_EXT: 0x%x\n",
